# Privacy Policy

_Last updated: August 13, 2026_

This Privacy Policy explains how MemoryBot collects, uses, stores, and deletes information when used in a Discord server.

## Overview

MemoryBot is a Discord bot that helps servers remember useful context from previous conversations. It works only in channels where a server administrator has explicitly enabled it.

MemoryBot is disabled by default. It does not collect memory from a server or channel unless an administrator runs `/enable`.

## Information Collected

When enabled in a channel, MemoryBot may process:

- Message content from enabled Discord channels
- Discord user IDs and user mentions
- Discord channel IDs and channel mentions
- Discord server IDs
- Message timestamps or related metadata
- Questions submitted through bot commands such as `/ask`
- Recent stored memory data used for `/catch-me-up`
- User opt-out status from `/ignore_me`

MemoryBot does not process direct messages. Bot commands are server-only and are not available in DMs.

## Information Stored

MemoryBot stores extracted memory summaries and related metadata in a local vector database.

MemoryBot does not permanently store full raw message transcripts as memories. Raw channel messages may be temporarily batched in memory so the bot can extract useful summaries, but the long-term stored data is the extracted memory summary and metadata.

Stored metadata may include server IDs, channel IDs, timestamps, and user IDs if configured.

## Use of AI Services

MemoryBot may send relevant message batches, questions, trigger-check messages, and stored memory text to Google Gemini for AI processing.

Gemini may be used to:

- Extract useful memories from channel discussions
- Generate embeddings for memory search
- Detect whether a message is asking about server memory
- Answer `/ask` questions
- Generate `/catch-me-up` summaries

The exact behavior may depend on the bot operator’s configuration.

## How Information Is Used

MemoryBot uses collected and stored information to:

- Remember useful server context
- Answer questions about previous discussions
- Summarize recent stored topics
- Detect when someone may be asking about past server context
- Provide server memory statistics
- Respect user opt-out choices

MemoryBot does not sell user data.

## Channel Controls

Server administrators can control where MemoryBot operates.

- `/enable [channel]` enables memory collection in a channel
- `/disable [channel]` disables memory collection in a channel
- `/forget confirm:True` deletes all stored memories for the server
- `/memory_stats` shows memory statistics

If a channel is not enabled, MemoryBot does not collect memory from that channel.

## User Controls

Users can opt out of memory collection in a server.

- `/ignore_me` stops MemoryBot from collecting that user’s messages
- `/unignore_me` allows MemoryBot to collect that user’s messages again in enabled channels

## Data Retention

By default, MemoryBot keeps stored memories for 90 days.

The bot operator may configure a different retention period. If retention is set to `0`, memories may be kept indefinitely.

MemoryBot runs a cleanup task every 24 hours while online to remove expired memories.

